\title{Masked vector load and store}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-15}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{language}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1003}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|simd::load<V>(p, m, passthrough)~} reads the lanes of a one-dimensional vector of numbers whose mask bit is set; the other lanes are not read and take \code{\verb~|passthrough~}. \code{\verb~|simd::store(p, v, m)~} writes the set lanes through a \code{\verb~|Ptr~}. With a tail mask from \code{\verb~|mask_first~} a loop reads and writes its last chunk without touching memory past the end. See [memory](design-simd-vectors-memory). \pr{1003}.}
